{"id": "z1015", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The best way to handle unexpected costs when traveling is to have money. Having some extra funds on hand gives you flexibility to cover surprise expenses like transportation issues, last-minute activities, or emergencies without having to worry about depleting your entire budget. While options like flying an airplane might be faster in certain situations, they don't directly address financial preparedness. Similarly, spending frivi lously can lead to overspending, and just going somewhere or relying on energy won't help with managing costs. So the most practical answer is E: have money.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 23, "carrier_ended": null}
