{"id": "z1775", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Steven has 19 peaches, and Jake has 1 2 fewer peaches than Steven. So we' ll subtract 1 2 from 19 to find out how many peaches Ja ke has. That's 19 minus 1 2, which equal s 7. So Jake has 7 peache s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1783", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "At the arcade, Dave had won 18 tickets. He used five to buy some toys and then another 11 for clothes. So that' s a total of 5 plus 11, which is 16 tickets spent. If you subtract that from his original 18, he would have 2 tickets left.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 17, "carrier_ended": null}
