{"id": "z2031", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, that' s a really good question. And the answer is probably both. So you have DNA virus es like poxvirus es that are actually quite hyper mutable. They have mechanisms of mut ation that allow them to mutate faster than other viruses.And then there's also RNA vi ruses which are known for their high mutation rates because they don't use proofread ing during replication and so they accumulate more errors in their genomes over time. So influenza and HI V are examples of highly mutable RNA virus es.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
