{"id": "z2271", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Genetic disorders are caused by mutations in our DNA, which can lead to problems with how the body functions. One example is al captonuria, a condition where the body cannot properly break down certain amino acids, leading to an accumulation of harmful substance s that can affect the urine and sweat. Another is albin ism, which results from a lack of pigment in the skin, hair, and eyes due to a defect in melanin production. These conditions often follow patterns of inheritance, such as recess ive or dominant genes, meaning they may skip generations or appear more frequently depending on whether both parents carry the affected gene. So, the answer would be A, rec essive inheritance has, because many genetic disorders like these require two copies of the defective gene for symptoms to appear.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 42, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2279", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "An increase in the demand for money in the economy could result from a higher price level. When prices rise, people need more money to buy goods and services, which increases the demand for money.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2287", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 35, "onset_chunk": 34, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is C. A contingent remainder based on whether or not the cousin has air s. When a man conveys property to his wife's cousin and the air s of his body, he creates a fee simple interest in the cousin but also an executory interest that includes a remainder contingent upon the existence of those air s. Later, when he convey s the same property to his niece in fee simple, she takes subject to the earlier execut ory interest. If the cousin later dies without air s, then the condition for the remainder fail s, and the executory interest will pass to whoever holds it at that time—likely the man’s heirs or the state, depending on the law. However, until the co usin dies with or without air s, the ni ce has only a contingent remainder. So the best answer is C.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 45, "carrier_ended": null}
